## 0. Verdict

PASS

No product fix. `cli/cmd_pm_launch.oo` has no `test -e`, no `sys_exec`, and no `sh -c`.
`--exec` after an ok gate calls `run_oodac_run` with the CAS leaf path as one list token.
Did not edit `host_run.oo`. Did not edit `pm_launch.oo`. Did not write the dirty parent.

## 1. W3-S1 no payload shell

  File: `cli/cmd_pm_launch.oo` (125 lines).
  git diff deletes:

    sys_exec(sys, "sh", "-c", "test -e " + sq(path) + "; exit 0")

  Live `--exec` block:

    if leaf == "" or path does not end in `.oo`: `launch_die("exec")`
    `rargs` is one item: the host path
    `run_oodac_run(fs, sys, rargs)` then `return`

  Grep of that file for `test -e`, `sh -c`, `sys_exec`, and `sq(` is empty.
  Quote stays in `cli/host_run.oo` `sq`.
  `run_oodac` starts `oodac` with `sh -c` and `sq` tokens.
  The payload path is one quoted argv to `oodac run`.
  It is not `sh` of the `.oo` file and not `sh -c` of CAS bytes.
  ELF and an empty leaf die with `exec` before that call.

## 2. W3-S6 gate before child

  Order on disk:

    1. name empty -> `missing package name`
    2. `pm_name_ok` fail -> `refuse name`
    3. no lock line -> `not installed`
    4. slurp leaf and hash (`body` only for `pm_cas_id`)
    5. `pm_launch_gate(sha, live, grant, need, yanked)`
    6. gate not `ok` / `ok ` -> `launch_die` (exit 2)
    7. then `--exec` or path print

  Gate strings are unchanged (`cli/pm_launch.oo`, 26 lines, not edited):

    yank -> `err yank`
    sha mismatch -> `err sha256 mismatch`
    extra caps -> `err caps`
    else `ok`

  Fail does not reach `run_oodac_run`.
  Fail does not print `ooda launch: ok` or `{"ok":true`.
  Helper `pwd` / `ls` in `pm_root_abs` and `pm_list_dir` still use `sh -c`.
  Those helpers are not the payload child. They run before the gate.

## 3. W3-S2 / W3-S3 caps subset

  Call is `pm_caps_ok(grant, need)`.
  `grant` is `ooda.pkg` `caps`. Worktree grant is `FsRead`.
  `need` is the lock cap field.
  `pm_caps_ok(parent, child)` is `(child & parent) == child`.
  Need must be a subset of grant. Extra lock bits are `err caps`.
  Arguments are not swapped.
  Proof: `cli/pm_extract_proof.oo` (`grant=1, need=2` -> `err caps`).
  Launch does not mint Process, FsWrite, or Net.
  It does not add a C spawn API. Child is the existing `oodac run` path.

## 4. W3-S4 no OODA_FS_WRITEDIR widen

  `cli/cmd_pm_launch.oo` does not name `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`.
  `run_oodac` sets `OODA_SRC_ROOT`, `OODA_COMPILER`, and `OODAC_BIN` only.
  `oo_child_filter_env` keeps parent `OODA_` / `OO_` keys.
  Unset stays unset (write deny). `/`, `$HOME`, and CAS are not assigned.
  Smoke may set the jail to `$PWD`. Launch does not grow that jail.

## 5. W3-S5 no CAS body print

  `body` is slurped once and passed only to `pm_cas_id`.
  No `println(body)`.
  Prints are:

    `ERR\tpm\t` plus a short tail
    `ooda launch: ` plus the same tail
    path-only: `ooda launch: ok ` plus the path
    `--json` (not `--exec`): keys `ok`, `cmd`, `name`, `path`

  `--exec` returns after `run_oodac_run`. It does not print ok first.
  Gate fail never prints the JSON object.
  Path and sha hex are allowed. Bytes are not printed.

